<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5310" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅμμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅπτω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>anything tied</i> or <i>made to
				tie:</i> hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>knot,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fist.</u>
				4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅ. λύειν, ἀπάπτειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.98
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅ. ποιεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					5.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>noose, halter,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				781
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>cord,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				696
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Steril.</u>
				244
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅ. παρθενίας</span>
			maiden <i>girdle,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				7.182
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				164
			</span></i> (Antip.), imitated in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				248.8
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Philomelium</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>link</i> of chain, <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>Or.</u>
				2.32d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b> in pl.,
				<i>clinches</i> in wrestling, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.143
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Fab.</u>
				23
			</span></i>; of the <i>wrestler's arms,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>6.</b>
			<i>measure of length</i> (like our <i>chain</i>), =
			<i><span class="en">
				40
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πήχεις,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hero
			</span></i>
			<i>*Geom.</i><i><span class="en">
				23.14
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				669
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>that which kindles,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.504
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
